## 1. Summary

- **Question:** with a limited retention budget, which customers should receive an offer when both churn risk and economic value count?
- **Answer:** rank customers by expected net value of an offer (p(churn) x save rate x value - cost), let an optimiser pick the customer-offer combination within budget, and size the budget where the marginal return falls below {{ recommendation.hurdle_marginal_roi | pct(0) }}.
- **Impact (test split, same {{ budget.base | usd }} budget):** {{ strategy_label | lower }} {{ chosen.expected_net_value | usd }} vs {{ c.risk.expected_net_value | usd }} for risk-only targeting (+{{ headline.delta_vs_risk | usd }}); label-based check of the targeting gain {{ unc['ev minus risk'].label_based_simulated_net | usd }} (95% interval {{ unc['ev minus risk'].lower_95 | usd }} to {{ unc['ev minus risk'].upper_95 | usd }}).
- **Budget:** {{ recommendation.recommended_share | pct(0) }} of the base (validation rule) gives {{ recommended.expected_net_value | usd }} on test from {{ recommended.cost | usd }}.
- **Main risk:** the save rate is assumed. Break-even {{ be.break_even_default_save_rate | pct }} vs assumed {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }}; a randomised pilot measures it before scale-up.

