## 6. Decision logic and results at the fixed budget

**Value proxy:** monthly charges x margin {{ cfg.value.margin | pct(0) }} x discounted months, with a base horizon of {{ cfg.value.base_horizon_months }} months scaled by tenure ({{ cfg.value.tenure_factors.new }} / {{ cfg.value.tenure_factors.developing }} / {{ cfg.value.tenure_factors.loyal }}) and a {{ cfg.value.discount_rate_annual | pct(0) }} annual discount rate. It is a 12-month truncated value, not a lifetime value.

**Expected value of an offer:** p(churn) x save rate x value - (offer cost + contact cost); offer cost is charged to every contacted customer (unconditional credit), which is conservative.

**Selection:** a mixed-integer knapsack (scipy/HiGHS) maximises total expected value subject to the budget, one offer per customer, offer eligibility and a {{ cfg.campaign.max_contact_share | pct(0) }} contact cap; customers with non-positive EV are never contacted. With one offer and equal costs, sorting by EV is provably optimal and is used directly.

**Offers:** a synthetic catalog of four offers with eligibility rules ([assumption register](../docs/assumption-register.md#offer-catalog)). On validation, segment offers beat the single standard offer by {{ decisions.strategy_selection.relative_gain | pct(0) }}, above the {{ cfg.campaign.strategy_selection.min_relative_gain | pct(0) }} rule, so the recommended rule is **{{ strategy_label | lower }}**.

